# Migrations are checked out with Unix line endings on every platform.
#
# Not a matter of taste: five of them insert text — the Blind-Date rules among it — and a
# migration file checked out with CRLF seeds that text *with* carriage returns. The same
# migration therefore produced different rows on a Windows checkout than on the Linux server,
# and the difference is invisible: same wording, same line count, four bytes longer, and a
# different checksum. It cost an hour to establish that nobody had edited anything.
#
# The rule is narrow on purpose. Everything else keeps Git's usual behaviour, so this does not
# quietly reformat the rest of the repository.
database/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
